# A state of the round-up interval as a default interval Interval<T, 1> (docs/developer/design/upward.md,
# "Conversions"): [-n, u], and the empty set (NaN, NaN) as the default empty set (+inf, -inf). Exact,
# in every rounding mode: the same set, the signs of zero bounds aside. Requires the rounding mode
# upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang
# -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_to_interval_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
output:        zl
output:        zu
requires:      upward xu xn
ensures:       same_set zl zu from=xu,xn
min_precision: 1
source:        the negated lower bound negated, and the upper bound, the empty set after a test (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   both bounds are selected after a test of the empty set; same_set states what comes out for every canonical state

e  = unord(xu, xu)
nl = neg(xn)
mi = neg(const inf)
zl = select(e, const inf, nl)
zu = select(e, mi, xu)
